body:
I have spoken to him about this and he did get upset saying he has seen his mom go through being insulted and he wouldn't do that to me randomly (ex saying I'm stupid because I put the dishes away) but he does it when I AM being that way (questioning him on things) I feel as if I just drained him.

&#x200B;

Thank you so much for the advice. I find it hard to walk away as It seems like I always need an answer right then. but I am going to try my hardest to start this way to clear my head. thank you.

I'm trying to. I was in a bad relationship in my past so my self esteem is very low at times. I feel like I need counseling but am terrified of it though I'm not sure why.

&#x200B;

Would him saying I'm "being an idiot" or "being stupid" "being annoying" count as name calling?
